{"Title":"An Act relative to continuing education requirements for any person holding a license as a real estate broker or salesman","BillNumber":"H366","DocketNumber":"HD3279","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"jwm1","Name":"Joseph W. McGonagle, Jr.","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jwm1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:42:00.783"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"jwm1","Name":"Joseph W. McGonagle, Jr.","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/jwm1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-20T11:42:00.7833333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H366/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative McGonagle of Everett, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 366) of Joseph W. McGonagle, Jr., relative to continuing education requirements for persons holding licenses as real estate brokers or salesmen.  Consumer Protection and Professional Licensure.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 87XX1/2 of chapter 112 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting at the end of the first paragraph the following two sentences:-\r\n\tThe board may authorize any courses or programs for continuing education credit which satisfy the provisions of this section.  The board may adopt such rules and regulations as it deems necessary for the continuing professional education required for renewal of licenses.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J17","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J17"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}